B = [
('Coleman','North America','1940s-present','outdoor',"In the style of Coleman, friendly vintage Americana outdoor utility. Baked enamel in sage and olive green with cream and tan trim, finished in a slightly worn painted-steel look with small dents and rust freckles. Rounded steel edges, sturdy rolled seams, brass and chrome details and khaki canvas in heavy weave. A bold red rounded-rectangle badge holds white lettering in a chunky slanted script with a thin white outline, repeated on cream plates and red and white woven labels. Secondary graphics are simple green and cream box colour-blocking with small red accents. Honest, dependable, nostalgic, family-friendly and built to be used hard."),
('Snow Peak','East Asia','2000s-present','outdoor',"In the style of Snow Peak, calm Japanese minimalism with refined metal craft. Brushed titanium, satin stainless steel, dark cast iron and pale natural wood combined in slim, precise, softly rounded geometric forms that stack, nest and pack flat. Palette is silver, charcoal, black, sand, olive and off-white with very sparse colour. The emblem is a simple black asterisk-like star of radiating lines, set in plain black or white with a thin lowercase wordmark and tiny descriptive line beneath. Surfaces are matte and uncluttered, edges are thin and clean, and joints are neat and understated. Quiet, thoughtful, tidy and made to last."),
('Shimano','East Asia','1980s-present','engineering',"In the style of Shimano, precise Japanese industrial engineering in a cool technical palette. Satin silver-grey and polished aluminium finishes meet gloss black and anodised dark grey, with fine machined facets, crisp chamfers and smooth sculpted curves. Graphics are small, exact and laser-etched or screen-printed in white or black. The wordmark is wide, rounded, bold blue capitals, often with a thin green stripe or blue and white horizontal bands. Surfaces carry tiny serial-style numbers, neat symbol icons and subtle colour-coded marks in blue, green and red. Clean white boxes with blue banding and product-line grids. Efficient, trustworthy and dense with quiet detail."),
('Campagnolo','Europe','1960s-80s','engineering',"In the style of Campagnolo, classic Italian racing refinement in jewel-like metalwork. Mirror-polished and satin silver aluminium and chrome with fine engraving, scalloped cut-outs, drilled patterns and hand-finished machining marks. The emblem is a small winged roundel in a rounded shield, shown embossed in pewter-look metal or printed in blue, gold and yellow on oval decals with a flowing handwritten script wordmark. Colours are deep royal blue, lemon yellow, red and cream with silver, often in oval or lozenge shaped badges and green or red frames. Ornate yet precise, nostalgic, proud, mid-century craft with a collectable patina."),
('Brompton','Europe','1980s-present','engineering',"In the style of Brompton, compact, clever British engineering with a playful modern twist. Slender round steel-like tubing, tidy brazed joints and hinged forms packed into neat compact blocks. Glossy solid colours in lime, orange, turquoise, sky blue, racing red, black and white, often with a contrast accent on a few details and silver or black metal fittings. Lettering is thin, wide-spaced uppercase sans-serif, engraved or printed small along slim surfaces, with a friendly rounded lowercase wordmark in orange on clean white and bright colour fields. Quirky, practical, urban, precise and optimistic, with tidy, minimal outlines and bold single colours."),
('Montblanc','Europe','1920s-present','luxury',"In the style of Montblanc, stately Swiss-German luxury in black and gold. Deeply polished black resin with a mirror depth, fine gold-plated and platinum-look rings, and satin silver metal in rounded, smooth, tapering forms. The emblem is a white six-pointed rounded star like a snow-capped peak, set inside a thin circle on black or silver, with widely spaced classical serif capitals in white, gold or silver. Fine pebbled and saffiano-like black leather with gold stamping, neat contrast stitching, burgundy and brown tones, and dark gift boxes with silver or gold foil. Executive, discreet, precise, timeless and confident, with heavy polished craftsmanship."),
('Parker Pens','North America','1940s-60s','stationery',"In the style of Parker Pens, streamlined mid-century American optimism and polished engineering. Smooth tapered torpedo forms, gentle bullet curves and slim arrow-shaped accents standing proud from the surface. Glossy lacquer in burgundy, deep blue, forest green, jet black, grey and cream, with fine herringbone, vertical line and pinstripe engraving. Brushed steel, gold-filled and chrome metal bands in thin rings. Graphics include a small arrow motif, a script wordmark in flowing cursive or slim upright capitals and a small blue diamond mark. Presentation boxes in satin-lined colour-blocked cards with thin gold rules. Refined, reliable, confident and quietly glamorous."),
('Lamy','Europe','1960s-present','stationery',"In the style of Lamy, rigorous German modernist industrial design. Simple geometric solids, smooth cylinders, flat planes and strict uncluttered proportions with a single slim flat bar as an accent. Matte, fine-grained black, charcoal, white and satin brushed stainless steel, with bright saturated tones such as red, yellow, blue, lime and orange in plain solid blocks. Faceted surfaces, small round windows and subtle recessed details are the only ornament. The wordmark is an extra bold, wide, slanted black sans-serif in capitals, often cropped large against white. Packaging is plain white or black card with sparse type and generous empty space. Functional, honest, disciplined, school-like and modern."),
('Staedtler','Europe','1900s-present','stationery',"In the style of Staedtler, orderly German technical and classroom precision in strong blue. Deep cobalt and navy blue paired with black, white and a few sharp accents of red, yellow and green, used in crisp flat bands and stripes on smooth lacquered surfaces. The emblem is a stylised white silhouette of a helmeted head in profile inside a solid blue square, beside a bold wide capital sans-serif wordmark set on white or blue. Packaging is clean, boxy and grid-based, with rows of tiny capital type, thin ruled lines, small flags and tidy coloured tabs. Natural kraft and pale wood tones appear in limited editions. Neat, reliable, practical, methodical and cheerfully educational."),
('Faber-Castell','Europe','1800s-present','stationery',"In the style of Faber-Castell, scholarly European heritage in deep green and gold. Dark forest and emerald green lacquer with matte and satin depth, paired with ivory, cream, black, brown and warm metallic gold or silver foil. The emblem shows two knights on horseback inside a small crest, with a refined serif wordmark in wide-spaced capitals and a tiny founding-year line beneath, in white on dark green. Surfaces feature fine hot-foil stamping, subtle embossing, rows of graded colour in neat ordered fans and polished wood, knurled metal and dark leather for luxury lines. Tins and boxes are dark green with gold lettering. Classic, craftsmanlike, dignified and warm."),
]
